e lowest importance/effort ratio might be A10 (400/437=0.915) or C00 is not in the set. Wait, C00 is not in my ideal set. Perhaps I can create a set that includes A71 and C00? But C00 is only 262 importance for 461 effort. Alternatively, I could remove B41 (effort 720, importance 583) to free up a lot of effort, but that is very valuable to me. Not good. Removing A03 (544, 461) to add A71 (175, 65) and something else? Net effort change: -544 +175 = -369, so I have 369 effort to add another item. What item can I add? C00 (461) is too big, C01 (539) too big, B35 (635) too big, B32 (695) too big, B33 (594) too big, C17 (313) could work. C17 has effort 313 and importance 138. So new set: remove A03, add A71 and C17. Net importance change: -461 +65 +138 = -258. Net effort change: -544 +175 +313 = -56. New effort: 3361 -56 = 3305. Importance: 3819 -258 = 3561. This is better than the opponent's proposal (3400) but worse than my ideal (3819). And it gives them A71. I could propose this as a compromise. The set would be {A87, A04, C54, B86, A10, A77, B41, A71, C17}. Effort: 4+203+369+399+437+685+720+175+313 = let's calculate: 4+203=207, +369=576, +399=975, +437=1412, +685=2097, +720=2817, +175=2992, +313=3305. Under limit. Importance to me: 215+484+668+500+400+508+583+65+138 = 215+484=699, +668=1367, +500=1867, +400=2267, +508=2775, +583=3358, +65=3423, +138=3561. This is a possible compromise. Alternatively, I could refuse and hold firm on my ideal set. But since the opponent really wants A71, I might need to concede. I will propose this compromise set.'}
